  {
   "type": "heading",
   "text": "Welcome, Scientist!"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "markdown": "This is a **check-in**, not a test.\n\nScientists are curious and not afraid to guess.\n\nShow us what you know and where you are curious to learn more."
  },
  {
   "type": "image",
   "emoji": "🧪",
   "alt": "Science time! We will visit matter, water, food chains, forces, light and sound.",
   "caption": "Science time! We will visit matter, water, food chains, forces, light and sound."
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "text": "Stop 1: Solids, liquids and gases"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "markdown": "Matter comes in three main states. A **solid** keeps its shape. A **liquid** flows and takes the shape of its container. A **gas** spreads out to fill all the space.\n\nHeating can **melt** a solid or **boil** a liquid. Cooling can **freeze** a liquid. Water freezes at 0 °C and boils at 100 °C."
  },
  {
